<title>BELGIUM: DANISH OFFICIAL TO RUN EU CEREALS/SUGAR DIVISION.</title>
<headline>DANISH OFFICIAL TO RUN EU CEREALS/SUGAR DIVISION.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish official Lars Hoelgaard has been appointed European Commission director of cereals, oilseeds, sugar and other crops, Commission officials said.</p>
<p>The appointment, which takes effect from September 1, includes chairing important weekly meetings of the EU cereals and sugar management committees which adjudicate export tenders and set market policy.</p>
<p>Hoelgaard, who as a former director of public and animal health was a prominent figure during the crisis over mad cow disease, replaces Spaniard Jose Manuel Silva, who has been promoted to become a deputy director general of agriculture.</p>
<p>Silva replaces another Spaniard, Fernando Mansito, who has taken an EU posting in Bosnia.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
